  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Position",
      "text": "Drawer can be placed on `left` (default), `top`, `right` and `bottom`. Control drawer position with `position` prop,\nfor example `<Drawer position=\"top\" />`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Offset",
      "text": "Set `offset` prop to change drawer offset from the edge of the viewport:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Customize overlay",
      "text": "`Drawer` uses [Overlay](/core/overlay/) component, you can set any props that [Overlay](/core/overlay/)\nsupports with `overlayProps`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sizes",
      "text": "You can change drawer width/height (depends on `position`) by setting `size` prop to predefined size or any valid width,\nfor example, `size=\"55%\"` or `size={200}`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Remove header",
      "text": "To remove header set `withCloseButton={false}`",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Change transition",
      "text": "`Drawer` is built with [Transition](/core/transition/) component. Use `transitionProps`\nprop to customize any [Transition](/core/transition/) properties:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "onExitTransitionEnd and onEnterTransitionEnd",
      "text": "`onExitTransitionEnd` and `onEnterTransitionEnd` props can be used to run code after\nexit/enter transition is finished. For example, this is useful when you want to clear\ndata after drawer is closed:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Initial focus",
      "text": "`Drawer` uses [FocusTrap](/core/focus-trap/) to trap focus. Add `data-autofocus`\nattribute to the element that should receive initial focus.\n\nIf you do not want to focus any elements when the drawer is opened, use `FocusTrap.InitialFocus`\ncomponent to create a visually hidden element that will receive initial focus:\n\nIf you do not add `data-autofocus` attribute and do not use `FocusTrap.InitialFocus`,\ndrawer will focus the first focusable element inside it which is usually the close button.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Control behavior",
      "text": "The following props can be used to control `Drawer` behavior.\nIn most cases it is not recommended to turn these features off –\nit will make the component less accessible.\n\n- `trapFocus` – determines whether focus should be trapped inside drawer\n- `closeOnEscape` – determines whether the drawer should be closed when `Escape` key is pressed\n- `closeOnClickOutside` – determines whether the drawer should be closed when user clicks on the overlay\n- `returnFocus` – determines whether focus should be returned to the element that was focused before the drawer was opened",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "react-remove-scroll settings",
      "text": "`Drawer` uses [react-remove-scroll](https://github.com/theKashey/react-remove-scroll)\npackage to lock scroll. You can pass props down to the `RemoveScroll` component\nwith `removeScrollProps`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Change close icon",
      "text": "Use `closeButtonProps` to customize close button:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Compound components",
      "text": "You can use the following compound components to have full control over the `Drawer` rendering:\n\n- `Drawer.Root` – context provider\n- `Drawer.Overlay` – render [Overlay](/core/overlay/)\n- `Drawer.Content` – main drawer element, should include all drawer content\n- `Drawer.Header` – sticky header, usually contains `Drawer.Title` and `Drawer.CloseButton`\n- `Drawer.Title` – `h2` element, `aria-labelledby` of `Drawer.Content` is pointing to this element, usually is rendered inside `Drawer.Header`\n- `Drawer.CloseButton` – close button, usually rendered inside `Drawer.Header`\n- `Drawer.Body` – a place for main content, `aria-describedby` of `Drawer.Content` is pointing to this element",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Drawer.Stack",
      "text": "Use `Drawer.Stack` component to render multiple drawers at the same time.\n`Drawer.Stack` keeps track of opened drawers, manages z-index values, focus trapping\nand `closeOnEscape` behavior. `Drawer.Stack` is designed to be used with `useDrawersStack` hook.\n\nDifferences from using multiple `Drawer` components:\n\n- `Drawer.Stack` manages z-index values – drawers that are opened later will always have higher z-index value disregarding their order in the DOM\n- `Drawer.Stack` disables focus trap and `Escape` key handling for all drawers except the one that is currently opened\n- Drawers that are not currently opened are present in the DOM but are hidden with `opacity: 0` and `pointer-events: none`\n- Only one overlay is rendered at a time\n\nNote that `Drawer.Stack` can only be used with `Drawer` component. Components built with `Drawer.Root`\nand other compound components are not compatible with `Drawer.Stack`.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "useDrawersStack hook",
      "text": "`useDrawersStack` hook provides an easy way to control multiple drawers at the same time.\nIt accepts an array of unique drawers ids and returns an object with the following properties:\n\nExample of using `useDrawersStack` with `Drawer` component:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fixed elements offset",
      "text": "`Drawer` component uses [react-remove-scroll](https://github.com/theKashey/react-remove-scroll)\npackage to lock scroll. To properly size these `elements` add a `className` to them ([documentation](https://github.com/theKashey/react-remove-scroll#positionfixed-elements)):",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "`Drawer` component follows [WAI-ARIA recommendations](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/dialog-modal/examples/dialog) on accessibility.\n\nSet `title` props to make component accessible, will add `aria-labelledby` to the content element:\n\nTo set close button `aria-label` use `closeButtonProps`:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
